WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:05.820
The Scarlet Rot is one of the deadliest&nbsp;
things in the Lands Between, for it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:12.840
no real cure....Even the demigods, could not&nbsp;
stave off its effects. I guess no one told&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:17.640
them about preserving boluses, huh? 
Anyway, what's really interesting about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:23.160
the Scarlet Rot, is that it's a very&nbsp;
old legend. One that predates Malenia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:29.880
and all of the horrors found in Caelid. 
And so, to understand where it all began, we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:35.940
to go below. To the Lake of rot, where we can find&nbsp;
a few item descriptions that speak of this time:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:42.120
for example, here in the southeastern corner,&nbsp;
we can loot a crown of mushrooms that forms a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:49.920
towering headpiece. And it reads: "Long ago, great&nbsp;
lords served the Scarlet Rot. Perhaps such fungal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:56.040
bodies served as their crowns". And the rest of&nbsp;
this set is made up of the Mushroom Set, which are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.040 --> 00:01:02.160
considered "holy vestments for those enraptured by&nbsp;
the scarlet rot, that root them to the earth". 
&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:08.760
So already, we have a hierarchy of mushroom&nbsp;
lords that served the Scarlet Rot, as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:14.520
as worshippers who venerated it. And you might&nbsp;
think it strange that these beings would worship,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:19.560
or serve a sickness...but the Scarlet&nbsp;
Rot is so much more than that.
&nbsp;

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:25.680
Because the Scarlet Rot is no mere disease.&nbsp;
No. For proof of that, one need only look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:31.500
at the Crystalian. Crystalian are inorganic&nbsp;
beings, and yet they can be afflicted by the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.820
Rot like any other. There's even some&nbsp;
crystalian that are infused with rot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:41.520
and can spread it to others, as well. 
Because it's not really a disease. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:47.940
the map for the Lake of Rot calls it the "divine&nbsp;
essence of an outer god". Something that "is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:53.460
sealed away" in this underground world. f you've been following Elden Ring lore&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.120
for any length of time, you should be no&nbsp;
stranger to the concept of an Outer God.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.120 --> 00:02:04.560
They are these indeterminable, abstract beings&nbsp;
that impress an order or will upon the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:10.500
through avatars, servants and vessels.
And in the case of the Scarlet Rot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:16.860
its order is one of decay, where beings are put&nbsp;
into a progressing state of death, with the intent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:24.000
to achieve the glorious rebirth that will follow.&nbsp;
The Poison Armament description tells us this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:30.000
saying that "those who dwell within poison know&nbsp;
rot all too well. The death that begets life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.420
that comes to all equally. That is to say: it&nbsp;
is the cycle of rebirth, put into practice". 
&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:42.300
We see this in places like Miquella's Haligtree,&nbsp;
which might be completely dead were it not for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:49.320
the fungal growths that have sprouted upon the&nbsp;
tree, and in Caelid, where flowers of the rot are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:56.820
on the very precipice of budding. Of course, it's&nbsp;
debateable whether this type of life is desirable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:04.080
but you can't argue that it IS life. And the&nbsp;
agents of the Rot God certainly find it desirable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:10.080
so they do their utmost to spark this&nbsp;
sacred cycle of rebirth in others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:19.200
infecting them with poison and rot.
On that note, there is one extremely curious item&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:25.140
that you can find down in the Grand Cloister..and&nbsp;
it's called the "Scorpion's Stinger". This is a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:32.040
dagger, glistening with Scarlet Rot, that is&nbsp;
called a "ceremonial tool". Which means any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:38.040
ceremony that used this dagger would have been&nbsp;
a ceremony to stab and infect another being with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:43.800
the Scarlet Rot. A ceremony of spreading&nbsp;
their treasured affliction to others. 
&nbsp;

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:49.680
But what's really interesting about this dagger,&nbsp;
is that it's fashioned from a "great scorpion's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:57.180
tail", and is also specifically said to have&nbsp;
been crafted from "the relic of a sealed outer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:04.140
god". And given that phrasing..it sounds like it's&nbsp;
saying that the dagger was fashioned from a relic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:14.460
of the Rot God, who was a Great Scorpion. Many&nbsp;
historical relics in our history are often the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:21.420
physical remains of deceased saints or holy&nbsp;
persons, so the God of Rot might really be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:28.980
or at least have manifested as a great scorpion.&nbsp;
So I guess this scorpion stinger is sort of like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:39.300
the eye of the fell god, or the three fingers of&nbsp;
frenzy, or the winged theme of death. It's a small&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:46.800
remaining hint at the visual identity of these&nbsp;
ephemeral outer gods, intended to stimulate the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:51.360
imagination, even if we never truly find&nbsp;
out what these Outer Gods look like. 
&nbsp;

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:57.900
But whatever Rot truly looks like, it, and its&nbsp;
Scarlet Rot essence, was eventually conquered,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:04.560
or "sealed". This was done by a legendary&nbsp;
figure, known as the Blind Swordsman. 
&nbsp;

00:05:04.560 --> 00:05:08.940
As the story goes, the blind&nbsp;
swordsman was favoured by a fairy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:14.700
called the "dancer in blue". The fairy&nbsp;
bestowed upon them a Flowing Curved Sword,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:21.180
which was patterned after flowing water, and with&nbsp;
this sword, the blind swordsman "sealed away an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:29.100
ancient god. A god, that was Rot itself". 
There's quite a bit to unpack here. First,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:35.700
who, or what, was the fairy, called the&nbsp;
Blue Dancer? Well, I think the warrior's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:41.520
Blue Cloth Set gives us a clue: It reveals that&nbsp;
the blue color of its fabric "symbolises brisk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:47.880
waters"..and the cloth doll that is the Blue&nbsp;
Dancer is styled to look just like water.  
&nbsp;

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:53.040
The description goes on to say that&nbsp;
"just as still waters turn foul,&nbsp;

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:59.820
stagnation leads to decay". So, "Warriors&nbsp;
must remain ever drifting". Therefore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:05.340
flowing water is the antithesis to Rot,&nbsp;
which thrives in stagnant water. 

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:12.600
And I think - and this is just speculation - but&nbsp;
I think the blue fairy might essentially be a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:18.840
sort of river spirit. If you've ever seen Hayao&nbsp;
Miyazaki's "Spirited Away", you might know what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:24.780
type of being I'm talking about. In that movie,&nbsp;
a stinking sludge monster comes to the bathhouse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:31.680
where it is eventually revealed that he's actually&nbsp;
a river spirit, whose river was bogged down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:37.860
corrupted by pollution. And once his waters&nbsp;
are unblocked, the river spirit is restored.
&nbsp;

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:46.440
Elden Ring, by comparison, does have two legendary&nbsp;
rivers, called the Siofra and the Ainsel, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.440 --> 00:06:53.100
just so happen to flow underground, next to, and&nbsp;
around the Scarlet Rot that was eventually sealed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:57.720
all that time ago. So I don't think it's&nbsp;
a stretch to think that this "Blue Fairy"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:04.560
might have occupied, or been a supernatural&nbsp;
extension of those underground rivers. I think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:10.260
its a fun theory, and it helps to explain the&nbsp;
Blue Fairy's relationship with water, and why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:16.500
it might be a natural enemy of the Rot god. So the Blue Fairy gave the Blind Swordsman a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:22.560
flowing sword, and he fought with the power of&nbsp;
flowing water to seal away the Rot God. What's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:29.880
unclear though, is how exactly the Scarlet Rot&nbsp;
god was sealed by the Blind Swordsman. Did he,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:36.780
sword in hand, battle a Great Scorpion boss&nbsp;
in one-on-one combat, and seal its essence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:43.320
away? Or was their battle more of an abstract&nbsp;
one, where the Eternal City dams were built&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:51.240
and rivers rerouted to encircle the rot&nbsp;
and contain it underground? These details&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.240 --> 00:07:57.120
are left to your imagination..but one way or&nbsp;
another, the Scarlet Rot was sealed away...

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:04.080
But it was not defeated. And eventually, it&nbsp;
would return. And this time, it would do so in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:10.200
an empyrean vessel - corrupting Malenia, Blade of&nbsp;
Miquella, at the very moment of her birth. 

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:25.680
Like her brother Miquella, Malenia was born&nbsp;
an Empyrean. Empyrean, meaning she was a valid&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:32.760
candidate to replace Queen Marika as a God, and&nbsp;
as such, it seems, a ripe candidate for an Outer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:36.900
God's meddling. It's unclear what mechanism the&nbsp;
Rot God used, but somehow, it was able to afflict&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:44.400
Malenia as soon as she was born. And that's&nbsp;
a shame, for Malenia's Great Rune does state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:49.740
that it should have been the most sacred&nbsp;
Great Rune "of them all", were it not for,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:55.680
what I assume, was the Rot God's meddling. And speaking of Great Runes - In the sister video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.680 --> 00:09:02.340
to this one, we talk about how Miquella was the&nbsp;
flip side to Malenia in many ways - especially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:08.940
in cut content, where the twins were "born of an&nbsp;
inseperable fate", and said to "hold the runes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:15.900
of both abundance and decay, between them". And&nbsp;
to reflect this, it seems, Miquella is in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:26.400
constant state of overflowing abundance, while&nbsp;
Malenia was in this constant state of dying. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:34.740
see this tragedy unfolding in a few statues of&nbsp;
Malenia, where she had all her limbs once upon a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:43.860
time, until the rot continued to take hold, moving&nbsp;
her inexorably towards her death, and rebirth. 
&nbsp;

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:50.280
And that death must have felt inevitable,&nbsp;
for in these early days, there were few known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:56.760
ways to ward off the rot. Fire was probably the&nbsp;
obvious one, and then there was also the act of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.760 --> 00:10:03.780
"consecration", which is the act of "declaring&nbsp;
something as sacred", which was done to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.780 --> 00:10:11.280
weaponry of Malenia and her knights; to help&nbsp;
their armaments, at least, resist the rot. 

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:16.800
But their flesh was still susceptible.&nbsp;
Malenia's knights were therefore called the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:22.500
"Cleanrot Knights", and they "vowed to fight&nbsp;
alongside Malenia, despite the inevitable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:29.220
if gradual, putrefaction of their flesh". And it&nbsp;
was this fact that made these warriors so fierce,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:34.920
for they had already accepted their&nbsp;
terrible fate, and so logically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:39.780
had nothing else to lose in battle.  
These knights were bestowed the Winged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:45.840
Sword Insignia, given only to those who fought&nbsp;
alongside Malenia the Severed. Interestingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:52.620
this is the only item to give Malenia the title&nbsp;
"the severed". I assume it's referencing a time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.620 --> 00:11:02.100
where Malenia was known for her prowess despite&nbsp;
her fragmented body, and it's possible that she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:07.020
wasn't yet known as the Blade of Miquella at this&nbsp;
time, though that's just my own speculation. 
&nbsp;

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:11.940
At any rate, "Malenia, Blade of Miquella" is&nbsp;
her most common title, and it's easy to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:18.480
why she would dedicate herself to her brother&nbsp;
so fully. For her brother was so dismayed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:22.740
her condition, that he dedicated himself&nbsp;
to finding a treatment for the Rot. 

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:28.680
And this search for a cure dramatically&nbsp;
affected Miquella's worldview. For instance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:38.880
he was formerly a faithful fundamentalist of the&nbsp;
Golden Order, but would abandon it, as it could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:45.360
do nothing to treat his sister's accursed rot.&nbsp;
Instead, he pursued a path of Unalloyed Gold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:51.540
and crafting for Malenia a needle that could&nbsp;
be inserted into her flesh, granting relief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.540 --> 00:11:56.400
from the rot, and preventing the progression&nbsp;
of the rotting sickness. If you're interested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:03.120
in WHY unalloyed gold works this way, then I'd&nbsp;
recommend you check out this video afterwards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:07.800
which talks at length about Miquella. 
We learn about Miquella's needle's specific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.800 --> 00:12:13.560
effects in-game, when we give it to a character&nbsp;
called Millicent, who is also suffering from the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:28.620
Scarlet Rot. Millicent has lost a limb, she&nbsp;
is losing her memories, and when we find her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:33.960
she is unable to even move. But as soon as we&nbsp;
give her the needle, she is able to function&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:39.840
and fight once more. Therefore, it's fair to&nbsp;
assume that similar benefits were conferred upon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.840 --> 00:12:44.760
Malenia when her brother gave her the needle. It's also worth noting that the multiple needles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:51.240
we find in-game aren't finished. Even the final&nbsp;
version can only be used in the storm beyond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.240 --> 00:13:11.700
time at Farum Azula, where it allows you to cheat&nbsp;
fate. Perhaps if Miquella had been able to imbue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:18.660
the needle with some time-warping capabilities,&nbsp;
he could have undone the effects of the Rot God,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:25.800
but again, the needle was never finished.
But the needle isn't all that Miquella created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.800 --> 00:13:33.660
with Unalloyed Gold. He also crafted for her a&nbsp;
prosthetic arm, leg, and helmet of unalloyed gold,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.660 --> 00:13:39.720
which, again, like Millicent, surely allowed&nbsp;
her to overcome her one-armed shortcoming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:46.440
and reach for new heights as a fighter.
So Malenia's prospects were already looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:52.920
up...but things didn't end there. For Malenia&nbsp;
would go on to meet a man who would become her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:59.820
mentor, and he would give her a final, invaluable&nbsp;
tool that could be employed against the Scarlet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:06.420
Rot. We see their meeting play out in the image&nbsp;
of the Prosthesis-Wearer Heirloom, which depicts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:12.240
"a scene from a heroic tale". You can even see&nbsp;
Malenia's prosthetic arm and leg if you look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:18.300
closely, which is why I assume this meeting&nbsp;
took place after Miquella's intervention. 
&nbsp;

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:27.480
Her mentor was, as you might have guessed,&nbsp;
the Blue Dancer - the man who first sealed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.480 --> 00:14:34.080
away the Rot, all those years ago. And after&nbsp;
encountering "her mentor and his flowing blade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:40.440
she gained wings of unparalleled strength". 
This meeting says a lot about the Blind Swordsman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:47.880
He must have known that Malenia was inhabited&nbsp;
by his ancient enemy, and yet he doesn't kill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:47.880 --> 00:14:54.060
her here - instead, he takes her under his wing,&nbsp;
and teaches her the techniques that he himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.060 --> 00:15:01.320
used to curtail the rot in the first place. It's a&nbsp;
pretty sage thing to do, and perhaps we shouldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:01.320 --> 00:15:05.940
expect any less from someone who was able to&nbsp;
defeat an Outer God in the first place. 
&nbsp;

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:12.900
So this is why the skill on Malenia's blade is&nbsp;
called the "waterfowl dance". This is why Malenia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.900 --> 00:15:20.340
recovers health by attacking during her boss&nbsp;
fight. By moving relentlessly, the damage of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:27.480
Rot was offset, and Malenia was able to achieve&nbsp;
unparalleled strength, and to maintain her pride.
&nbsp;

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:32.340
The same pride that she would&nbsp;
abandon, in her fight with Radahn. 

00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:45.120
Radahn was born of Queen Rennala, who was&nbsp;
the Queen of Caria, and King-Consort Radagon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.120 --> 00:15:50.880
who was previously a great champion of the&nbsp;
Erdtree. Thus was the order of the moon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:56.040
and the Erdtree, conjoined. And while Radahn was a true Carian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:02.760
and certainly proficient in the art of sorcery&nbsp;
- we can see in his character an inclination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:08.640
towards another path; an apsiration to&nbsp;
be like Godfrey, the first Elden Lord,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:15.000
and also his father Radagon, who would become&nbsp;
the second Elden Lord. Caria was, after all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:21.840
a largely matriarchal society, meaning that power&nbsp;
was passed down to the princesses in the family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:27.720
so perhaps it's no surprise that Radahn was&nbsp;
not as motivated by his Carian heritage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:34.020
compared to his sister Ranni, for example. So Radahn's set was decorated with a golden lion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.020 --> 00:16:40.140
that symbolized Godfrey and his beast regent, and&nbsp;
states that "from his youngest years, Radahn was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:44.580
naturally captivated by the Lord of the&nbsp;
battlefield". Then his golden helmet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.580 --> 00:16:49.200
was designed with his flaming red hair in&nbsp;
mind, which he inherited from his father,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:54.840
drawing attention to the fact that Radahn&nbsp;
was fond of the heroic implications of being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:54.840 --> 00:17:02.700
Radagon's son. He and his knights became known as&nbsp;
the "Redmane", which conflates Radagon's red hair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:08.940
with the mane of Godfrey's Lion, and Radahn was&nbsp;
even quoted as saying "I was born a champion's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:15.600
cub. Now I am the Lord of the Battlefield's&nbsp;
lion", which borders on being a statement of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:20.640
loyalty to Godfrey, and the Golden Order..but&nbsp;
we'll get to that debate a little later.

00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:28.500
So naturally, this was a guy who revelled in&nbsp;
warfare. And Even in his youth as a Carian Royal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:35.700
it seems Radahn was already a renowned general. We&nbsp;
can infer this because of a man named Jerren.

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:41.220
The Eccentric's Armor specifically says that&nbsp;
"after spending time as a guest of the Carian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.220 --> 00:17:47.400
royals, he became a guest commander for General&nbsp;
Radahn". Therefore, Radahn must have still been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:47.400 --> 00:17:54.540
close with his Carian family, as Jerren met Radahn&nbsp;
through these Carian royals. And when they did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.540 --> 00:18:01.680
meet, the two seemed to immediately share a&nbsp;
certain bond. For despite Jerren preferring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:01.680 --> 00:18:08.100
a nomadic existence, he decided to become a&nbsp;
guest commander for General Radahn. And then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:16.680
despite the temporary implication of such a title,&nbsp;
Jerren, "the restless tumbleweed", "would become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:16.680 --> 00:18:22.620
bound by honorable oath", and he and Radahn&nbsp;
swore a vow of honorable death to one another.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:28.500
Promising that they would die honorably in battle,&nbsp;
even if it was death by the other's hand.

00:18:29.580 --> 00:18:36.120
It's not stated which battles Radahn was fighting&nbsp;
at the time, nor which war he required a new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:40.500
"guest commander" for..but then, the world&nbsp;
was very different at the time, and there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:40.500 --> 00:18:45.240
so much of the Land's Between's history that we&nbsp;
don't know about. I guess it's possible that the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:52.080
battles were being fought for distant lands like&nbsp;
Limgrave, and Caelid? The Limgrave East Map does,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:57.300
after all, say that this path here was&nbsp;
"trod by many a soldier in the past".&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:57.300 --> 00:19:04.020
Maybe Radahn's forces took this path as well. 
This was before Caelid was even afflicted with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:08.280
Scarlet Rot..so things might have looked very,&nbsp;
very different at this time. Though admittedly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:08.280 --> 00:19:12.660
the only shot we have of this time was during the&nbsp;
war that Radahn fights in...aaaand it still does&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:12.660 --> 00:19:22.860
look like a bit of a red hellscape here. 
That said, Caelid did still hav some culture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:22.860 --> 00:19:29.520
to boast of. For example, in the very middle of&nbsp;
Caelid, long ago, there was a town of sorcery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:38.700
called Sellia. And despite Radahn's relationship&nbsp;
with Caria and Raya Lucaria, it was here in Sellia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:44.520
that he studied, learning gravitational magics&nbsp;
that likely could not be taught anywhere else.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:50.280
He did this, as the story goes, "all so he&nbsp;
would never have to abandon his beloved,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:58.500
but scrawny steed". For gravitational magics could&nbsp;
relieve the weight of Radahn and allow his horse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:01.980
to carry him evermore. 
Also, very important lore note:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:08.160
the horse's name is Leonard. Just letting you&nbsp;
know we're using that name going forward. 
&nbsp;

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:14.011
And what's interesting about Leonard, is that he's&nbsp;
specifically called out as being scrawny..rather&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:14.011 --> 00:20:26.280
than Radahn being called out as enormous. So I&nbsp;
think, personally, that Radahn didn't actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:31.560
become as large as he is for a very long time. And&nbsp;
there's some good evidence to back that up. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:37.920
one, his throne in Leyndell is of regular size,&nbsp;
two, his portrait is of a simple grown man, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:44.700
lastly, we see a brief shot of Radahn fighting in&nbsp;
this image, where he barely even matches Morgott&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:51.720
in size. So personally, I think Radahn only truly&nbsp;
grew in size when he acquired a great rune. 
&nbsp;

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:59.160
Anyway: so it's stated that Radahn initially&nbsp;
learned gravitational magic for the sake of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:05.580
his horse. But, that gravitational skillset would&nbsp;
certainly come in handy, as the years went on.
&nbsp;

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:10.860
For one, these gravitational magics were&nbsp;
passed on to some of his elite soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:18.000
like Ogha, who was the "longest-serving member&nbsp;
of the Redmane Knights", who "studied techniques&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:25.080
to manipulate gravity alongside Radahn"
Their equipment and skillsets really were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:31.440
very inspired by Radahn. For example, the surcoat&nbsp;
of Radahn's Redmane Knights depicts a red-maned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:38.880
lion raising a sword in the image of Radahn, and&nbsp;
"all proved they were worthy of the name". Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:46.140
greatshield takes it further, being shaped like&nbsp;
a fang, and featuring the crest of a red-maned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:52.860
lion. And they were strong like Radahn, too, with&nbsp;
descriptions stating that they were "reputed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:21:52.860 --> 00:21:58.020
be masterful warriors, and it was popularly&nbsp;
said that the Redmanes knew no weakness"
&nbsp;

00:21:58.020 --> 00:22:03.540
But for all their prowess in battle, it's&nbsp;
possible that a conflict was coming that no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:03.540 --> 00:22:15.240
mere soldiers could ward away. But luckily,&nbsp;
Radahn was able to solicit the help of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:15.240 --> 00:22:19.860
an extremely knowledgeable teacher.
According to the Gravity Well sorcery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:26.160
Radahn's master was an Alabaster Lord, with&nbsp;
skin of stone. And these onyx and alabaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:32.100
lords were a different race entirely, said&nbsp;
to have risen to life when a meteor struck&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:32.100 --> 00:22:39.660
long ago. The meteorite sorcery tells us that&nbsp;
they were called lords in "reverential fear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:39.660 --> 00:22:43.740
of their destructive power"...And I speculate that Radahn needed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:50.760
their help because a similarly meteoric meteoric&nbsp;
"destructive power" was on its way to Sellia.&nbsp;

00:22:51.600 --> 00:22:57.720
Earlier it was said that he explicitly learned&nbsp;
gravitational magic so that he could ride his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:22:57.720 --> 00:23:03.480
horse, but the collapsing stars sorcery also&nbsp;
explicitly says that he learned gravitational&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:03.480 --> 00:23:09.840
techniques so that he could challenge the stars,&nbsp;
which I think suggests that there were two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:09.840 --> 00:23:15.480
distinct periods of learning here for Radahn.&nbsp;
Learning for the sake of his horse, and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:15.480 --> 00:23:21.360
learning for the sake of keeping Sellia safe. There's quite a bit of evidence that suggests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:27.780
Radahn's actions here were in defense. The Sword&nbsp;
Gravestone in Caelid, for example, specifically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:33.720
tells us that Radahn "held Sellia Secure".&nbsp;
The Starscourge Heirloom tells us that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:33.720 --> 00:23:40.080
Radahn "confronted the falling stars",&nbsp;
as if they were the aggressors. Finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:40.080 --> 00:23:46.200
this event was called the "Starscourge&nbsp;
Conflict", suggesting there was a clash&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:46.200 --> 00:23:53.940
of some kind - a back and forth, if you will. So Radahn seemed to anticipate that this event was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:59.880
coming, but I guess that isn't so strange when&nbsp;
you consider that Radahn was of Carian lineage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:23:59.880 --> 00:24:07.980
who were renowned for reading fate in the&nbsp;
stars. So anticipating a starfall seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:07.980 --> 00:24:13.260
pretty straightforward, and it makes sense&nbsp;
that Radahn would want to intervene if it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:18.000
was headed for Sellia, which he learned&nbsp;
his magic from in the first place. 
&nbsp;

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:23.700
So..Radahn took defensive measures. And..I guess&nbsp;
you might even argue that he went a bit overboard.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:23.700 --> 00:24:30.780
For he didn't just defend Sellia, he actually&nbsp;
sealed the stars movements completely. 
&nbsp;

00:24:30.780 --> 00:24:38.700
So After Radahn challenged the stars, the fate&nbsp;
in the night sky was no more..which manifests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:38.700 --> 00:24:44.940
quite literally in Ranni's questline,&nbsp;
where Radahn has to be killed and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:44.940 --> 00:24:52.020
stars unfrozen so that one can smash into&nbsp;
Limgrave and open a path to Nokron. &nbsp;

00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:58.920
If not for Radahn, I'm pretty sure a star would&nbsp;
have smashed through Sellia instead, and opened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:24:58.920 --> 00:25:05.820
a path to Nokron that way all those years ago.&nbsp;
The Eternal City of Nokron is, after all, said to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:05.820 --> 00:25:18.240
"sleep below Sellia"...so Radahn really might have&nbsp;
intervened here at the very last moment. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:25.860
I'll admit it is strange that the star eventually&nbsp;
hits Limgrave, and not Sellia. I wonder why?&nbsp;

00:25:29.460 --> 00:25:37.800
You could also make the argument that Radahn&nbsp;
intervened here on behalf of the Golden Order.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:46.140
After all, the Telescope literally says that "the&nbsp;
fate once writ in the night skies" was "fettered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:46.140 --> 00:25:53.640
by the Golden Order". And Radahn was a fanboy&nbsp;
of Radagon and Godfrey, two proponents OF the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:53.640 --> 00:25:59.580
Golden Order, so it's definitely possible that&nbsp;
he did this on the Golden Order's behalf. 
&nbsp;

00:26:00.120 --> 00:26:05.580
Personally though, I think that both&nbsp;
things can be true. Radahn was clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:05.580 --> 00:26:12.000
motivated to defend Sellia from starfall,&nbsp;
AND the Golden Order stood to benefit from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:12.000 --> 00:26:17.700
one of its vassals achieving such a feat. 
But while Radahn, and most of the demigods at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:31.440
that stage, for that matter, were technically on&nbsp;
the side of Marika's Golden Order - the impression&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:31.440 --> 00:26:37.620
I get from Radahn is that he has no real loyalty&nbsp;
to anyone other than himself and his men.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:39.900 --> 00:26:44.820
I think this, because he's not really&nbsp;
hated by anyone in the current age.&nbsp;

00:26:45.900 --> 00:26:51.840
Even his brother Rykard has his picture&nbsp;
up on the wall, and Rykard famously hated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:51.840 --> 00:26:57.120
anything to do with the Golden Order. 
So while Radahn served the intent of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:57.120 --> 00:27:02.340
Golden Order, I don't think he was beholden&nbsp;
to it. Especially not in the later years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:02.340 --> 00:27:06.840
when the Elden Ring was shattered.&nbsp;
Remember this cutscene, with Morgott?

00:27:07.500 --> 00:27:13.680
Willful traitors, ALL. 
Morgott labels all the demigods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:13.680 --> 00:27:19.080
as traitors to the Golden Order. Including&nbsp;
Radahn, who we do see in a clash with Morgott,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:19.080 --> 00:27:23.760
suggesting that he might have abandoned his&nbsp;
loyalty to order, and marched on Leyndell. &nbsp;

00:27:24.780 --> 00:27:31.260
For Radahn, like his demigod kin, had claimed&nbsp;
a Great Rune. And it's easy to assume that a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:31.260 --> 00:27:38.280
warmonger like him would have great ambitions, and&nbsp;
might have even aspired to become Elden Lord. &nbsp;

00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:42.240
And it's around this time, when&nbsp;
the demigods were clashing - that&nbsp;

00:27:42.240 --> 00:27:48.480
Malenia enters the picture once more. 
Malenia, Blade of Miquella, was marching towards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:27:48.480 --> 00:27:53.517
Caelid. Past Godrick ... and Towards Radahn. 
&nbsp;

00:27:53.517 --> 00:27:56.760
Honestly, Godrick's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:01.380 --> 00:28:08.520
nothing more than a jumped up country&nbsp;
bumpkin. Lord? Don't make me laugh.

00:28:09.060 --> 00:28:12.540
First he hid himself amongst the&nbsp;
womenfolk to flee the capital,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:12.540 --> 00:28:19.260
then hid from Radahn in that castle...
Then he insulted Malenia, lost to her in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:19.260 --> 00:28:23.040
battle, only to lick her boots&nbsp;
rather than die like a man.

00:28:23.040 --> 00:28:27.720
Has he no shame, the big girl's blouse?

00:28:29.100 --> 00:28:34.260
This dialogue from Kenneth Haight is a great piece&nbsp;
of lore, as it tells us a lot about a crucial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:34.260 --> 00:28:39.000
late part of the shattering war.
At this point, Godrick had just failed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:44.520
to usurp Leyndell capital, and had fled with&nbsp;
his tail between his legs, to Stormveil. &nbsp;

00:28:44.520 --> 00:28:51.120
Here, he hid in fear. Of Radahn, who was&nbsp;
a close neighbour in Caelid. And it makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:28:51.120 --> 00:28:56.460
sense that he'd fear Radahn, who was considered&nbsp;
by many to be the strongest of the Demigods. 

00:28:56.460 --> 00:29:02.460
But while he was hiding here, a different army&nbsp;
approached. From the north, not the south,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:02.460 --> 00:29:08.040
as Godrick must have feared. Malenia and&nbsp;
her Cleanrot Knights were passing Stormveil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:08.040 --> 00:29:18.120
on their southwards march, which is marked&nbsp;
at the Liurnia Highway Sword Gravestones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:18.120 --> 00:29:23.400
which state "Nothing will hinder the wings of the&nbsp;
Blade of Miquella, and the Cleanrot Knights"&nbsp;

00:29:23.940 --> 00:29:30.720
These gravestones tend to mark points of battle,&nbsp;
and Kenneth does state that Godrick "insulted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:30.720 --> 00:29:37.080
Malenia" and "lost to her in battle", so&nbsp;
I assume this is where that happened. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:29:37.080 --> 00:29:42.120
to the nature of the insult..well we have cut&nbsp;
dialogue from Godrick to help us out here. &nbsp;

00:29:42.660 --> 00:29:49.200
There is only one tree, and only its branches.
That bathe in true rays of gold.
&nbsp;

00:29:49.200 --> 00:29:54.060
Not the fool Omen King.
Nor the rank malformed twins.
&nbsp;

00:29:55.320 --> 00:30:01.860
Godrick considered Miquella and Malenia "rank"&nbsp;
and "malformed". So I assume the insult was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:01.860 --> 00:30:07.620
along those lines..which was..not smart on&nbsp;
Godrick's part. Malenia must have messed him up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:07.620 --> 00:30:19.500
but tellingly, she did not kill him. And&nbsp;
that's a curious detail. Because if she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:19.500 --> 00:30:25.500
was seeking the power of others' Great&nbsp;
Runes in order to restore the Elden Ring,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:29.460
and live up to her or Miquella's empyrean promise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:29.460 --> 00:30:34.020
then you'd think that surely she wouldn't show&nbsp;
him mercy. Surely, she would have killed him?&nbsp;

00:30:36.600 --> 00:30:43.620
So to me, that suggests that Malenia was not&nbsp;
on a southward march to take power. If she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:30:43.620 --> 00:30:48.720
didn't claim Godrick's Great Rune, then she&nbsp;
probably wasn't here for Radahn's either.&nbsp;

00:30:48.720 --> 00:30:56.040
So then, why? Why did Malenia come full force&nbsp;
towards Radahn, on this southward march? 
&nbsp;

00:30:56.040 --> 00:31:00.480
I feel like there are three options. Four if&nbsp;
you count the theory that Malenia might have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:00.480 --> 00:31:05.460
chased down Radahn in order to get control of&nbsp;
the Elden Ring, but as I've just explained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:05.460 --> 00:31:09.600
I feel like that's unlikely. Option two, though it's still unlikely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:11.820 --> 00:31:16.200
might be that Malenia sought to fight Radahn&nbsp;
simply for the sake of fighting him. He was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:16.200 --> 00:31:21.960
after all, widely considered the mightiest of&nbsp;
the Demigods - as was Malenia, in many cases.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:21.960 --> 00:31:28.020
So it's not ridiculous to think that both of them&nbsp;
might have fought simply for the sake of pitting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:28.020 --> 00:31:33.900
their strength against one another, but this is a&nbsp;
pretty unsatisfactory answer, in my opinion. &nbsp;

00:31:33.900 --> 00:31:39.480
Option three I feel could be because Malenia&nbsp;
was looking for her brother. At this point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:39.480 --> 00:31:45.240
Miquella could have already been stolen away&nbsp;
by Mohg, so perhaps she was looking for him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:45.240 --> 00:31:52.800
She pretty intentionally makes a beeline to&nbsp;
the south, towards Caelid, and Mohg's palace&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:31:52.800 --> 00:32:01.260
is directly underneath Sellia, where an asteroid&nbsp;
was once supposed to hit..so I guess it's possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:01.260 --> 00:32:08.460
that Malenia had some intel leading her here,&nbsp;
though this is, of course, only speculation.
&nbsp;

00:32:08.460 --> 00:32:13.800
But my favourite theory is this fourth one, which&nbsp;
is that Malenia, and, by extension, Miquella,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:13.800 --> 00:32:19.980
may have wanted Radahn dead for the same reason&nbsp;
that Ranni eventually does. So that the stars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:19.980 --> 00:32:26.940
could resume their movement, bringing certain&nbsp;
fates back into play! But why would Miquella&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:26.940 --> 00:32:32.760
require the stars to resume their movement? 
Well, perhaps Miquella's own fate was locked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:32.760 --> 00:32:38.160
in stasis. We do find a demigod's amber&nbsp;
starlight shard in Miquella's hideaway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:38.160 --> 00:32:44.340
after all, and I feel like it should be concerning&nbsp;
that his fate might have fallen like this. 
&nbsp;

00:32:44.340 --> 00:32:51.420
Or perhaps Miquella wanted the stars&nbsp;
back in motion so that the moon could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:51.420 --> 00:32:55.860
properly eclipse the sun. This was a&nbsp;
ritual that Miquella seemed to believe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:32:56.580 --> 00:33:03.480
would revive Godwyn the Golden, which we&nbsp;
talk more about in this video - and I can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:03.480 --> 00:33:09.060
definitely see how the stars being in stasis&nbsp;
would prevent the moon eclipsing the sun. &nbsp;

00:33:18.120 --> 00:33:22.620
In the end though, there's only one answer&nbsp;
that I am confident in: and it's that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:22.620 --> 00:33:30.420
can't confidently say for sure why Malenia&nbsp;
fought Radahn. But whatever the reason, it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:33:30.420 --> 00:33:36.480
must have been a good one. For it was during this&nbsp;
battle, that she sacrificed ... everything.

00:33:45.060 --> 00:33:50.340
There is something I must return to Malenia.
The will that was once her own.
&nbsp;

00:33:50.340 --> 00:33:58.320
The dignity, the sense of self, that allowed&nbsp;
her to resist the call of the scarlet rot.
&nbsp;

00:33:58.320 --> 00:34:02.340
The pride she abandoned, to&nbsp;
meet Radahn's measure.

00:34:03.360 --> 00:34:08.580
In Elden Ring's story trailers, we see this&nbsp;
legendary fight play out. Cleanrot Knights&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:08.580 --> 00:34:12.360
finally arrive with Malenia, facing&nbsp;
off against the Redmane Knights, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:12.360 --> 00:34:18.240
manage to plunge many spears into Radahn during&nbsp;
their clash. You can actually still see these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:18.240 --> 00:34:23.700
spears sticking out of his back, to this day. Then, at some point, Malenia and Radahn appear to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:23.700 --> 00:34:28.860
be the only two left standing. Malenia sacrifices&nbsp;
her prosthetic arm to get close to Radahn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:28.860 --> 00:34:34.860
grabbing her blade, and plunging it into them&nbsp;
both, giving us a close-up view of the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:34.860 --> 00:34:41.280
characters. Here, Radahn looks monstrous, which&nbsp;
I theorise could be because he's "tainted with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:41.280 --> 00:34:46.020
the madness of a Great Rune", though that is&nbsp;
just speculation. We can also see Malenia's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:46.020 --> 00:34:52.020
lips moving here, muttering some final words or&nbsp;
perhaps the incantation for the Scarlet Aeonia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:34:52.020 --> 00:34:56.340
which envelops herself and Radahn,&nbsp;
putting an end to their fight. 

00:34:56.340 --> 00:35:02.220
In this videos first chapter, we spoke extensively&nbsp;
about Malenia's battle against the scarlet rot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:02.220 --> 00:35:10.740
within her - but in this moment, she lost&nbsp;
that fight, and allowed the Scarlet Rot to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:10.740 --> 00:35:19.500
take hold. Millicent calls this "sacrificing&nbsp;
her dignity, her sense of self, her will,&nbsp;

00:35:19.500 --> 00:35:25.560
and her pride". She did all of this, just&nbsp;
so that she could "meet Radahn's measure".&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:25.560 --> 00:35:31.380
Thus did the Scarlet Rot explode outwards,&nbsp;
infecting Radahn, and the very land itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:31.380 --> 00:35:38.700
as their battle came to a horrific standstill. 
In the end, neither party was in a state to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:38.700 --> 00:35:43.860
continue fighting. So technically, Malenia&nbsp;
didn't lose, so she was technically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:43.860 --> 00:35:48.120
still undefeated.
Few survived the battle of Aeonia,

00:35:48.120 --> 00:35:54.960
but one who did was the Cleanrot Knight&nbsp;
Finlay, who "in an unimaginable act of heroism,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:35:54.960 --> 00:36:01.560
carried the slumbering form of Malenia all the way&nbsp;
back to the Haligtree". They managed this alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:01.560 --> 00:36:07.800
fending off all manner of foes along the way 
But back at the center of Caelid, Malenia's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:07.800 --> 00:36:14.880
scarlet bloom remained.
Sublime, I tell you.
&nbsp;

00:36:14.880 --> 00:36:18.720
The very first flower of Aeonia&nbsp;
bloomed on this very spot.

00:36:18.720 --> 00:36:26.460
Malenia, may you blossom into a goddess.
In the present day Caelid features, at its center,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:26.460 --> 00:36:36.360
a giant tree that spirals in a similar manner&nbsp;
to Malenia's first scarlet bloom. As the phantom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:36.360 --> 00:36:41.880
says, this was the very first flower of Aeonia,&nbsp;
and the beginning of the scarlet swamp in this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:41.880 --> 00:36:48.420
land. And at the very center of that, is another&nbsp;
curious thing: A boss named Commander O'Niel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:54.840
who carries the Commander's Standard, which reads&nbsp;
"Even after his lord was fled, Commander O'Neil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:36:54.840 --> 00:37:01.560
continued to brandish this flag in the devastation&nbsp;
of the rot-eaten field of battle, the sole veteran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:01.560 --> 00:37:06.600
who remembers this battle with pride". 
It's hard for me to say exactly whose side&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:06.600 --> 00:37:13.500
O'Niel would have been on. He summons the spirits&nbsp;
of exiled soldiers, who themselves have no real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:13.500 --> 00:37:19.980
affiliation to speak of - though I will say 
you CAN summon one of Millicent's sisters to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:19.980 --> 00:37:26.760
help you in the fight against O'neil, which might&nbsp;
suggest that he's opposed to the idea of rot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:26.760 --> 00:37:43.200
and might have fought for Radahn. And when you defeat O'Neil by luring him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:43.200 --> 00:37:48.840
into the geysers of Scarlet Rot, because why not -&nbsp;
he doesn't just drop the Commander's Standard - he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:48.840 --> 00:37:55.560
also drops an heirloom of the battle of Aeonia.&nbsp;
A broken needle of unalloyed gold, that was once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:37:55.560 --> 00:38:01.500
buried within Malenia's own flesh..repelling&nbsp;
her scarlet rot..until it snapped. 

00:38:01.500 --> 00:38:07.320
An interesting question here, considering the&nbsp;
needle is broken, is whether Malenia snapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:07.320 --> 00:38:12.900
the needle intentionally when she plunged&nbsp;
her blade into herself and Radahn. Perhaps&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:12.900 --> 00:38:20.520
she knew that it would cause the rot within her&nbsp;
to flare up worse than ever, and allow her to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:20.520 --> 00:38:28.320
defeat Radahn. After all, Millicent comments&nbsp;
as such later in her questline, as well. &nbsp;

00:38:31.500 --> 00:38:37.920
I pause to even tell you, but...
I took out the needle myself.

00:38:37.920 --> 00:38:46.680
The scarlet rot writhes now, worse than ever. At any rate, the final moments of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:46.680 --> 00:38:51.960
battle must have taken place here, as we do find&nbsp;
Cleanrot Knights able to rise when you're near,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:38:51.960 --> 00:38:56.280
even now - but then...we don't&nbsp;
find Radahn anywhere near here.

00:38:56.280 --> 00:39:00.720
Instead, we find him closer to his&nbsp;
former home at Redmane Castle. 

00:39:00.720 --> 00:39:05.460
In a nearby catacomb, the spirits of&nbsp;
the war-dead actualy continue to clash,

00:39:05.460 --> 00:39:11.340
refusing to surrender, even in death. 
And outside, Radahn is exactly the same way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:11.340 --> 00:39:19.080
And while witless; he's still alive, even&nbsp;
managing to keep the stars in stasis. For&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:19.080 --> 00:39:24.600
he's still in possession of his Great Rune, which&nbsp;
itself started to burn, to resist the encroachment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:24.600 --> 00:39:30.180
of the Scarlet Rot". His feet have rotten off&nbsp;
... the spears of the Cleanrot Knights remain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:39:30.180 --> 00:39:38.880
in his flesh - but now he simply uses them as&nbsp;
arrows to fight off anyone who threatens him:&nbsp;

00:39:38.880 --> 00:39:44.700
Refusing to give up and die in&nbsp;
anything but an honorable death. &nbsp;

00:40:30.240 --> 00:40:35.880
As the rot takes hold, Caelid becomes a&nbsp;
fresh hell, and the land itself becomes&nbsp;

00:40:35.880 --> 00:40:39.300
a threat. Even the dragons in&nbsp;
this place were forced to flee,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:39.900 --> 00:40:43.440
making a new nest on a plateau that&nbsp;
would be dubbed "Dragonbarrow",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:43.440 --> 00:40:51.840
where no one else then dared to enter. That said,&nbsp;
a few dragons did not make it away unscathed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:53.040 --> 00:40:59.820
Ekzykes succumbed to the scarlet rot, though he&nbsp;
did not forget his hatred - and sadly, Greyoll,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:40:59.820 --> 00:41:06.960
the mother of all dragons, who dwarfs all -&nbsp;
can be found on death's door surrounded by her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:06.960 --> 00:41:17.160
children. Sad. Thanks for the 50k runes tho. And in the end, it was Malenia's Scarlet Rot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:17.160 --> 00:41:23.880
not Malenia herself, that would eventually&nbsp;
drive Radahn's Redmane Knights to defeat 

00:41:23.880 --> 00:41:28.380
According to their armor, when they were&nbsp;
driven to defeat by Malenia's scarlet rot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:28.380 --> 00:41:32.880
the Redmane Knights burned off the&nbsp;
crest on the left breast of their armor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:32.880 --> 00:41:40.020
to indicate their resolve, stating "Alas, dear&nbsp;
home, I shan't see you again! For our duty is to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:40.020 --> 00:41:46.380
remain here, a bulwark against the blight". 
The knights using fire to burn away their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:46.380 --> 00:41:52.380
crest in this way is a great symbol, for fire&nbsp;
was their one and only weapon for fighting back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:52.380 --> 00:41:57.720
against the rot. And interestingly, according&nbsp;
to the Armorer's Cookbook, a lot of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:41:57.720 --> 00:42:04.440
tools and techniques were passed down by an&nbsp;
armorer who served the great general Radahn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:04.440 --> 00:42:09.960
as his books "contain knowledge of dealing with&nbsp;
rot; the application of fire in particular".

00:42:09.960 --> 00:42:17.280
And so this "flame of the redmanes" clearly became&nbsp;
a large part of their identity henceforth. Corpses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:17.280 --> 00:42:23.700
of rabid wildlife were piled high and burned,&nbsp;
long smouldering walls of flame were build&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:23.700 --> 00:42:30.360
in order to prevent the rot from spreading to&nbsp;
neighbouring lands, and to their own castles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:32.100 --> 00:42:38.520
and they even managed to commandeer some flame&nbsp;
chariots to help in their fight, utilising&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:38.520 --> 00:42:44.460
torches, fire pots, arrows, and more. 
Fittingly, Knight Jerren's beloved sword,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:44.460 --> 00:42:49.980
a Flamberge, became the symbol of the&nbsp;
castle itself - thanks to the flame-like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:49.980 --> 00:42:57.540
undulation that gives the flamberge its name. And Jerren himself remained at Redmane Castle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:42:57.540 --> 00:43:04.020
to regularly host a celebration of war,&nbsp;
calling champions from far and wide to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:04.020 --> 00:43:11.100
deliver death. A death for his friend, who is&nbsp;
now festering with rot, and crippled by madness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:11.100 --> 00:43:18.720
who now only wishes for an honourable way out 
Meanwhile, amidst Malenia's aeonian butterflies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:18.720 --> 00:43:23.435
pale pests emerge from the Swamp of Aeonia and&nbsp;
as the rot spreads, so do they, drawn to any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:23.435 --> 00:43:27.240
land that is "afflicted by scarlet rot". 
And though they appear as mere bugs - they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:27.240 --> 00:43:34.380
not. These creatures are intelligent, with a quote&nbsp;
unquote "keen intellect" that allows them to craft&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:34.380 --> 00:43:43.800
uncanny weaponry from sharpened shell, incant&nbsp;
spells, and even tame wild beasts. That said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:43.800 --> 00:43:49.560
they are ultimately creatures of worship,&nbsp;
and Gowry actually calls them "witless",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:43:49.560 --> 00:43:55.680
which does contrast with them being described&nbsp;
as intelligent, in this item description. 
&nbsp;

00:43:56.940 --> 00:44:03.660
The pests are also called the "abandoned children&nbsp;
of the goddess", and "servants of the Goddess of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:03.660 --> 00:44:10.440
Rot", who have "been forsaken" . And it's not&nbsp;
hard to see why - not only was Malenia carried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:10.440 --> 00:44:20.700
far away at the very moment of her bloom, but&nbsp;
she resents and resists the Scarlet Rot - unless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:20.700 --> 00:44:30.720
she's pushed to the absolute brink. And who&nbsp;
wouldn't hate the pests? Is there anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:30.720 --> 00:44:35.640
more annoying than this bloody attack? 
Nevertheless, the pests persist. They even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:35.640 --> 00:44:40.620
have a quotable line of dialogue in the&nbsp;
Kindred of Rot's Exultation talisman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:40.620 --> 00:44:46.560
which reads "Rot for the scarlet goddess. O&nbsp;
scarlet blossoms, flourish in distant lands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:46.560 --> 00:44:52.740
and return to us, the unwanted children."
...which brings us to the phrase "Scarlet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:52.740 --> 00:44:56.482
Blossoms". This...might not just be talking&nbsp;
about the literal flower buds of the scarlet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:56.482 --> 00:44:56.582
rot..but instead, what if the scarlet blossoms are&nbsp;
actual people? What if they're the five sisters;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:44:56.582 --> 00:44:58.500
Polyanna, Maureen, Amy, Mary, and Millicent -&nbsp;
who are the flower buds of the scarlet rot?
&nbsp;

00:45:06.120 --> 00:45:19.680
The girl, Millicent. She is a bud.
Green and undeveloped,&nbsp;

00:45:19.680 --> 00:45:24.780
waiting to flower into magnificence.
What a wondrous day that will be.

00:45:25.380 --> 00:45:30.660
In truth, before her, I'd never seen&nbsp;
a bud of such superior quality.

00:45:30.660 --> 00:45:38.400
She might very well outshine her sisters.
So it seems that the pests, including Gowry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:39.060 --> 00:45:45.180
have a keen interest in cultivating these&nbsp;
scarlet blossoms. I'd prefer to talk about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:45.180 --> 00:45:52.080
Millicent's questline in a future Prepare&nbsp;
to Cry episode, so I'll hold off for now,

00:45:52.080 --> 00:45:58.920
but essentially, Gowry does this in anticipation&nbsp;
of the daughters becoming scarlet Valkyries,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:45:58.920 --> 00:46:12.840
who might one day serve Malenia when she&nbsp;
ascends as the goddess of rot. Stay tuned for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:12.840 --> 00:46:16.260
a good Prepare to Cry episode on that one. 
But Malenia hasn't been seen for a long while.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:16.260 --> 00:46:20.700
Not since she was carried off to&nbsp;
the Haligtree, and the Haligtree's&nbsp;

00:46:20.700 --> 00:46:25.500
location itself was a mystery to many. 
But there were still those who venerated,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:25.500 --> 00:46:32.640
and worshipped her. And they weren't all pests.&nbsp;
Some of them were human, like Maleigh Marais,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:38.640
the castellan of the Shaded Castle. 
Maleigh wears the Marais mask, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:38.640 --> 00:46:44.340
something only worn by the head of House Marais.&nbsp;
It bears the likeness of the first of their line,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:44.340 --> 00:46:51.600
and describes the long, dual history of the&nbsp;
Marais family, who served as both executioners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:51.600 --> 00:46:57.540
and castellans of the Shaded Castle. 
So, fittingly, their storied sword is the Marais&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:46:57.540 --> 00:47:03.120
Executioner's Sword - a broad-bladed weapon..that&nbsp;
would eventually be used against them. 

00:47:03.120 --> 00:47:10.320
For one day, they made the mistake of capturing&nbsp;
a Bell-Bearing Hunter, named Elemer. But Elemer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:10.320 --> 00:47:15.420
who knew battle skills that allowed him&nbsp;
to move objects with his very own will,&nbsp;

00:47:15.420 --> 00:47:21.060
snatched the sword from the site of his looming&nbsp;
execution, and overthrew his captors. &nbsp;

00:47:21.060 --> 00:47:26.520
But it doesn't seem like he wanted to rule over&nbsp;
the castle in their stead. Instead, the castle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:26.520 --> 00:47:33.480
falls into ruin...and when we find him, Elemer is&nbsp;
just standing and staring at an enormous portrait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:34.200 --> 00:47:39.540
a picture of Malenia, who some believe is&nbsp;
to blame for the fate of the castle. 

00:47:42.120 --> 00:47:49.800
House Marais is ruined... Just deserts,&nbsp;
for falling for that severed harpy. No&nbsp;

00:47:49.800 --> 00:47:53.880
surprise that guilty cretin took the&nbsp;
castle and our storied sword...

00:47:53.880 --> 00:47:58.620
In the outskirts of the castle, you can&nbsp;
actually find and fight Maleigh Marais,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:47:58.620 --> 00:48:04.380
the former castellan of the castle, who has&nbsp;
now been ousted. He wields the Antspur Rapier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:04.980 --> 00:48:10.560
a weapon that evokes the Scorpion Dagger we&nbsp;
mentioned at the start of the video - as it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:10.560 --> 00:48:18.360
also a blade fashioned from a chitenous creature -&nbsp;in this case, a giant ant. Fittlingly then,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:18.360 --> 00:48:24.240
its description reminds us that "Scarlet&nbsp;
Rot is an old legend", and goes on to state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:24.240 --> 00:48:30.780
that "Maleigh Marais of the Shaded Castle was a&nbsp;
private believer in the Scarlet Rot. And indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:30.780 --> 00:48:39.780
he eventually found his own personal goddess." The Marais Robe explains why, stating that "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:39.780 --> 00:48:46.200
sons of House Marais are all sickly born", and&nbsp;
so "Maleigh Marais was beguiled by the beautiful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:46.200 --> 00:48:53.340
and fierce goddess who was born into rot".&nbsp;
Malenia was, after all, powerful and fierce&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:48:53.340 --> 00:48:59.400
in spite of her affliction, so it's easy to&nbsp;
see why Maleigh Marais looked up to her. 

00:48:59.400 --> 00:49:04.260
Though I guess it's possible that he took&nbsp;
this veneration too far, as the castle is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:04.260 --> 00:49:09.480
found sinking into a poison swamp..aaaand&nbsp;
the throne room is filled with prosthetics,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:09.480 --> 00:49:15.900
which mirror Malenia's own. Indeed, it's&nbsp;
possible he even found Malenia's own prosthetic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:15.900 --> 00:49:21.420
as you can loot the Valkyrie's Prosthesis&nbsp;
here, which reads "Golden prosthesis once&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:21.420 --> 00:49:27.420
used by the one-armed valkyrie. A masterwork of&nbsp;
craftsmanship, with practice and skill it can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:27.420 --> 00:49:32.640
be used as proficiently as a real arm. When&nbsp;
Maleigh Marais, Lord of the Shaded Castle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:32.640 --> 00:49:38.460
embraced this prosthesis, he claimed to feel&nbsp;
the presence of his personal goddess."

00:49:39.180 --> 00:49:44.820
Now I'm not sure if this is Malenia's actual&nbsp;
prosthesis or not. I feel like you could make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:44.820 --> 00:49:51.900
debates for and against that, but regardless, it&nbsp;
drives home just how much of a fanboy he was.

00:49:51.900 --> 00:49:58.320
But in the end, the castle is not much more now&nbsp;
than a home for some surviving Cleanrot Knights,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:49:58.320 --> 00:50:02.070
who would understandably feel&nbsp;
at home in this place ...

00:50:02.070 --> 00:50:07.320
and I guess they don't have much else to do,&nbsp;
as Malenia slumbers, back at the Haligtree. 
&nbsp;

00:50:07.320 --> 00:50:15.240
Where she does little else until you arrive,&nbsp;
and trigger her second transformation.
&nbsp;

00:50:22.440 --> 00:50:27.960
Wait.
The scarlet bloom flowers once more.

00:50:29.040 --> 00:50:35.520
You will witness true horror.
Now, rot!

00:50:36.540 --> 00:50:41.580
Now, I've got some bad news for you guys in&nbsp;
this final chapter. So...I know how difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:41.580 --> 00:50:47.100
Malenia was to defeat. But ... what if I&nbsp;
told you that wasn't her final form?

00:50:48.600 --> 00:50:54.240
For the Scarlet Aeonia description reads&nbsp;
"Each time the scarlet flower blooms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:50:54.240 --> 00:50:59.820
Malenia's rot advances, and with the third&nbsp;
bloom, she will become a true goddess". 

00:51:00.720 --> 00:51:06.180
It's known that Malenia's first bloom was in&nbsp;
Caelid. And we know she blooms in a fight against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:06.180 --> 00:51:13.140
us. So the debate becomes - is this mid-fight&nbsp;
bloom Malenia's second bloom, or her third?
&nbsp;

00:51:13.800 --> 00:51:18.420
Some would argue that this is Malenia's&nbsp;
third bloom, and that she's already become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:18.420 --> 00:51:23.520
the Goddess of Rot. She does, after all,&nbsp;
literally have "Goddess of Rot" as her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:23.520 --> 00:51:29.640
title. And there is a bloom right outside,&nbsp;
which could have been the site of her second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:29.640 --> 00:51:35.280
bloom. So how do you argue against that?
Well, for starters, the bloom outside might&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:35.280 --> 00:51:40.560
not be hers. For one, it'd be weird if she&nbsp;
had a second bloom that is never described,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:40.560 --> 00:51:46.620
right here...when she's slumbering in just the&nbsp;
neighbouring room, but not only that, In front&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:46.620 --> 00:51:52.620
of this bloom, you actually loot the traveller's&nbsp;
set, which is the same set worn by Millicent and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:51:52.620 --> 00:52:00.360
her sisters. Considering Millicent and her sisters&nbsp;
are buds of Malenia, and considering Millicent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:00.360 --> 00:52:06.300
also leaves behind one of these buds when she&nbsp;
dies, it's not ridiculous to think that one of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:06.300 --> 00:52:12.060
these might have flowered here already.
And I don't think Malenia having "Goddess&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:12.060 --> 00:52:18.360
of Rot" in her boss title means that&nbsp;
much. Many, like Gowry and the pests,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:18.360 --> 00:52:24.120
already believe Malenia is the Goddess of Rot.&nbsp;
The Scarlet Aeonia description instead specifies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:24.120 --> 00:52:30.900
that the third bloom will make her a "true"&nbsp;
goddess, and I think anything before that is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:30.900 --> 00:52:37.380
a brief flash of the Rot god shining through. 
The biggest piece of evidence that Malenia hasn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:37.380 --> 00:52:43.980
reached her third bloom yet, in my opinion, comes&nbsp;
from Gowry - who goes to extraordinary lengths to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:43.980 --> 00:52:51.120
nurture Millicent, encouraging us to kill her,&nbsp;
just so she can turn into a budding flower,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:52:51.780 --> 00:52:57.360
with her true potential unlocked henceforth. 
It must be done by your hand; no other.
&nbsp;

00:52:57.360 --> 00:53:05.880
Millicent trusts you, rather deeply in fact.
Sever that trust. Nurtured by betrayal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:05.880 --> 00:53:11.220
her bud will flower most vividly.
When Malenia ascends to godhood,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:11.220 --> 00:53:16.860
Millicent too shall be reborn.
As a scarlet valkyrie.
&nbsp;

00:53:17.640 --> 00:53:23.640
If Millicent dies, she flowers, with Gowry's&nbsp;
expectation being that she will be revived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:23.640 --> 00:53:29.640
after this. So considering there's a bloom in&nbsp;
Malenia's room that appears after you defeat her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:29.640 --> 00:53:35.820
I feel like she could have another&nbsp;
revivification after this, as well. 
&nbsp;

00:53:36.420 --> 00:53:40.980
One final piece of evidence was actually pointed&nbsp;
out by you guys in the comments of my recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:40.980 --> 00:53:47.340
Oracle short. In that video, I argued that the&nbsp;
Oracles might be there to herald the return of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:47.340 --> 00:53:52.920
Miquella as a god, as their spirit ashes state&nbsp;
"It is said that when Oracle Envoys appear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:53:52.920 --> 00:53:57.120
playing their pipes, they do so to herald&nbsp;
the arrival of a new god, or age."
&nbsp;

00:53:57.120 --> 00:54:03.360
But I completely neglected to mention that...they&nbsp;
might be here to herald Malenia's ascension&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:03.360 --> 00:54:05.968
as a god, instead. Thanks to you guys for

00:54:05.968 --> 00:54:13.080
pointing that out. If you haven't already, I'd appreciate if you gave my shorts content&nbsp;a shot, by the way. It's extremely difficult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:13.080 --> 00:54:17.340
to fit everything in 60 seconds, but&nbsp;
it's a fun challenge, and there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:17.880 --> 00:54:22.830
some great short stories in there&nbsp;
that I think you'll enjoy. 

00:54:22.830 --> 00:54:26.460
So I personally wouldn't be surprised&nbsp;
if we fight some incarnation of Malenia&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:26.460 --> 00:54:33.300
again in the DLC..and I'd be down for that&nbsp;fight, provided she rises again with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:33.300 --> 00:54:38.280
lower half as a scorpion, or something. 
But what I find to be the most disturbing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:38.280 --> 00:54:45.180
thought about Malenia's third bloom though,&nbsp;is that Gowry believes a scarlet bloom will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:45.180 --> 00:54:55.080
be more vivid if it's nurtured by betrayal. 
So what if Malenia's third bloom could be more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:54:55.080 --> 00:55:03.060
vivid..if she's betrayed by her brother?
But it's late, and I'm really getting into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:03.060 --> 00:55:09.480
deranged speculation territory now, aren't I?&nbsp;
That's probably my cue to end the video. 

00:55:10.020 --> 00:55:15.660
Special thanks to mispap for the footage and&nbsp;
editing help, as always, and special thanks to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:15.660 --> 00:55:20.760
Quelaag, as well, for looking over this script,
And thank you, as always, for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:55:20.760 --> 00:55:21.260
watching. 

